# ZenTen Pomodoro App - Project Structure Guide

This is a React-based Pomodoro timer application with the following architecture:

## Main Entry Points

- [src/index.jsx](mdc:src/index.jsx) - Application entry point with React StrictMode and RouterProvider
- [src/router/index.jsx](mdc:src/router/index.jsx) - React Router configuration with protected routes
- [vite.config.js](mdc:vite.config.js) - Vite build configuration with path aliases (`@` → `src/`)

## Directory Structure

- `src/components/` - Reusable React components organized by feature (Layout, Tasks, Timer, etc.)
- `src/pages/` - Page-level components (Home, Pomodoro, Profile, Auth pages)
- `src/store/` - Zustand state management stores (auth.js, tasks.js, journals.js)
- `src/db/` - Database layer with Supabase client and API functions
- `src/utils/` - Utilities, constants, transformers, and shared components
- `src/styles/` - Global CSS with variables and reset styles
- `src/assets/` - Static assets including SVG icons

## Key Technologies

- **Frontend**: React 19, React Router, CSS Modules
- **State Management**: Zustand with shallow comparisons
- **Database**: Supabase with API layer and data transformers
- **Build Tool**: Vite with path aliases and SVG-as-React components
- **Styling**: CSS Modules with CSS custom properties (design tokens)
- **Icons**: SVG files imported as React components via `vite-plugin-svgr`

## Authentication Flow

- Protected routes use [src/router/ProtectedRoute.jsx](mdc:src/router/ProtectedRoute.jsx)
- Auth state managed in [src/store/auth.js](mdc:src/store/auth.js)
- Session management through Supabase auth APIs

## Component Organization

- Each component directory contains `index.jsx` and `style.module.css`
- Sub-components organized in nested directories
- Feature-based grouping (Tasks, Timer, Layout, etc.)
